  "@type": "SemioticProjection",
  "instance_name": "semiotic_projection_1",
  "label": "User projected onto the scene of execution",
  "description": "The user is projected onto the execution scene, where the visual of a man being hanged and the overlaid text ('traitors', 'pure evil', 'bring back the gallows!', 'she never thought she would lose. until she did') collectively create an immersive experience that invites the user to identify with the narrative of retribution and moral victory. The phrase 'she never thought she would lose. until she did' implies a personal or collective experience of betrayal and downfall, which the user is invited to project themselves onto. The scene, as a whole, functions as a container for the user's emotional and ideological identification.",
